  "rationale": "One of Kenny Burrell's most celebrated Blue Note sessions, Blue Lights is a powerhouse jam-session date with a murderer's row of sidemen: Louis Smith, Tina Brooks, Junior Cook, Duke Jordan, Bobby Timmons, Sam Jones, and Art Blakey. Originally issued as two volumes (BLP 1596/1597), it captures Burrell at the peak of his early hard-bop period \u2014 a catalog of guitar blues, soul-jazz grooves, and swinging standards. The all-star cast (particularly Art Blakey's incendiary drumming) and the legendary Alfred Lion / Rudy Van Gelder production make this a defining Blue Note date of the late 1950s. AllMusic gives it 4.5\u2605, DownBeat 4\u2605. While Burrell is already in the canon via Midnight Blue, Blue Lights is his second defining statement and belongs alongside it.",
